1
00:00:02,558 --> 00:00:07,228
The parish garden feast is bright,
Linden trees rustle and sigh.

2
00:00:07,366 --> 00:00:11,882
Glasses clinking in the light,
Underneath the summer sky.

3
00:00:11,935 --> 00:00:16,236
And the sun is hanging so low,
Warm in the parish yard today.

4
00:00:16,596 --> 00:00:21,181
With glasses and laughter to flow,
And music to carry away.

5
00:00:22,953 --> 00:00:27,675
Laughter drifting through the heat,
People crowded in the shade.

6
00:00:27,837 --> 00:00:32,447
Children running on light feet,
To the music that is played.

7
00:00:32,463 --> 00:00:36,996
The priest with a beer in his hand,
His cigarette smoke curling high.

8
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:41,898
He watches us both as we stand,
Underneath the late afternoon sky.

9
00:00:43,544 --> 00:00:47,940
Luna stands alone upon the grass,
Talking to the priest nearby.

10
00:00:47,962 --> 00:00:52,435
He smiles and raises up his glass,
Underneath the summer sky.

11
00:00:52,514 --> 00:00:57,296
He says, "He is a lovely boy,
You make a handsome pair, it's true."

12
00:00:57,395 --> 00:01:02,340
Luna laughs and smiles with quiet joy,
"As long as he behaves, I do!"

13
00:01:14,044 --> 00:01:18,706
We sit at the table so long,
Our families sharing the space.

14
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:23,528
Grandparents hum to the song,
A smile on my grandmother's face.

15
00:01:23,703 --> 00:01:28,271
My mother is knitting a thread,
"A sweater for Luna," she plans.

16
00:01:28,281 --> 00:01:33,063
With your hand on my back as you tread,
Our dream is right here in our hands.

17
00:01:34,345 --> 00:01:39,222
But Albert talks of the sun,
Four weeks in a far, distant land.

18
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:43,590
The freezing in me has begun,
I tightly grip hold of your hand.

19
00:01:45,098 --> 00:01:49,588
Your mother is trembling with fear,
"She’s never been gone from my side."

20
00:01:49,707 --> 00:01:54,163
One week is the deal we get here,
While shadows are starting to glide.

21
00:01:55,704 --> 00:02:00,512
One week is the boundary they draw,
The first stone of cages is laid.

22
00:02:00,522 --> 00:02:04,995
A whisper of what I foresaw,
A debt that has got to be paid.

23
00:02:05,906 --> 00:02:10,902
"You're not worth it," the shadow-voice groans,
As the afternoon light starts to fade.

24
00:02:11,004 --> 00:02:15,503
The walls are built of cold stones,
And we walk to the darkening shade.

